From b234a1e37a3487095e91203e89f4b7807f563852 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Schwinn Saereesitthipitak <schwinns@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:24:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] [KV Connector] Restore NIXL P/D workers independently
 from process checkpoints

Lets prefill and decode workers be checkpointed and restored independently,
and several replicas be restored from one checkpoint.

- Each restore appends a random suffix to the KV engine id, so peers
  handshake again instead of reusing metadata cached by engine id. The
  engine passes the new id to the workers.
  MultiConnector children always share the engine's id, and a restore
  copies the new one into each child's config. A child that sets its own
  engine_id now gets a clear error instead of a TypeError.
- Once UCX is initialized in a process, a checkpoint of it cannot be
  restored, even after the agent is destroyed: UCX keeps process-wide
  network state, such as routes by interface index. So NIXL supports
  process checkpoints only with --checkpoint-prepare-on-startup, and its
  workers then create their agent at checkpoint restore and register the
  KV cache when it wakes. Every agent gets the backends and UCX backend
  params of the first. A worker that already had an agent, as in a
  prepare and restore in one process, drops the old agent's peers, gets a
  new one and republishes its handshake metadata under the new engine id.
  NixlBaseConnector.engine_id now reads the config, so it follows restores.
  Preparing again after a restore logs a warning, since that checkpoint
  cannot be restored.
- The NIXL scheduler stops its handshake listener on prepare and records
  which interface carries the side-channel host. Restore keeps that address
  if the pod still has it, and otherwise takes a routable address of the
  same interface. Names such as DNS names are kept. A listener that cannot
  bind fails startup or restore instead of hanging.

--checkpoint-prepare-on-startup is refused for an in-process engine core,
which never prepares, so NIXL workers there would never create an agent.

Out of scope: NIXL push mode and the P2P offload tier.

Signed-off-by: Schwinn Saereesitthipitak <schwinns@nvidia.com>
(cherry picked from commit ba0dd0c26ed0590c8f21b148423a39ff5fa6c870)
